;
; How Chainman files a corner in its land hierarchy, in MYRA
; (chainman_rules.h CH5): the survey, the parcel in it and the corner of
; the parcel, then the corner's place on the survey grid, x east and y
; north in millimetres. The model asks whether the numbers fit before it
; writes the field book.
^ZXCHAIN(survey:i6, parcel:i6, corner:i4) = x:i7! ^ y:i7!
